A thread that joins a ring is not linked from the newest thread before it.
A signal or a switch would never reach it, and the ring would not close;
a queue is a ring linked both ways.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: a waiting or ready thread is on no queue
Report: queue is not linked back

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -95,7 +95,7 @@ static void ring_push(paddr_t *head, paddr_t self, size_t off)
         struct links *oldest = links_at(*head, off);
         s->next = *head;
         s->prev = oldest->prev;
-        links_at(oldest->prev, off)->next = self;
+        (void)links_at;
         oldest->prev = self;
     }
 }
